  IWM: passed on 6 candidates — Closest to taking was the 2026-10-16 310/314 call credit spread ($108 credit, $292 risk, 71.5% POP), the one candidate whose direction matches the desk's bearish rate/PCE lean. What stopped it: expectancy on its own stated numbers is roughly 0.715 x $108 - 0.285 x $292 = -$6 per contract, before ~$5 of entry slippage and ~$15 of round-trip friction at $7.50/leg/contract, and max_qty of 1 means that friction cannot be amortised. The top-scored 283/279 put spread is worse still (-$38 expectancy per contract) and leans bullish against the catalyst read. Selling premium at hv_rank 14 across a 50-day window containing two CPI/PCE prints and a live FOMC is bottom-decile compensation for event-dense risk. Flat book, no carry cost to waiting.
