[13:40:38] scan
  SPY: passed on 6 candidates — Came closest to the 2026-10-16 772/768 put credit spread (score 59.72, $180 max gain vs $220 max loss). What stopped me: the 0.4526 short delta — the 772 strike is already 18c in the money against spot 771.82, so this is a 55.4% coin flip dressed as premium selling, and its 59.7 score leans entirely on a bias_fit of 1.0 for a bullish trend the catalyst read just downgraded to neutral (Hammack hawkish, further Fed speech pending, $3.8B SPY outflow). At one contract the round-trip friction is ~$15 plus $3.50 entry slippage against $180 theoretical max gain that requires holding 50 days through two CPI prints and an FOMC — and the book is already long index beta via the QQQ 765/775 call spread, so short SPY puts is size on the same factor, not diversification. The high-POP alternatives are worse arithmetic: 805/815 needs 85.1% wins at 83% POP, and the 825-wing structures ($1,734/$1,774 max loss) breach the $1,000 per-position cap outright.
