  QQQ: passed on 6 candidates — Pass, and the number that decides it is max_qty = 0: the book already holds the QQQ 765/775 call credit spread and max_positions_per_underlying is 1, so every candidate on this menu is rejected outright rather than trimmed — any qty >= 1 fails the concentration gate. The one I came closest to was the 2026-10-16 700/747 iron condor (top score 54.01, only bias_fit 1.0 against the neutral catalyst read, $294 credit on $506 defined risk); even absent the gate its 0.398 terminal POP and $26 entry slippage on a worst leg quoting 2.9% wide with 8 lots of daily volume left roughly 9% of the credit on the table at the click, and its 0.3185-delta short put only 2.8% below spot would have stacked index short-gamma on a one-day-old position that hasn't yet cleared Jackson Hole. Correct action is to let the existing 765/775 spread work.
      note: passed: Pass, and the number that decides it is max_qty = 0: the book already holds the QQQ 765/775 call credit spread and max_positions_per_underlying is 1, so every candidate on this menu is rejected outright rather than trimmed — any qty >= 1 fails the concentration gate. The one I came closest to was the 2026-10-16 700/747 iron condor (top score 54.01, only bias_fit 1.0 against the neutral catalyst read, $294 credit on $506 defined risk); even absent the gate its 0.398 terminal POP and $26 entry slippage on a worst leg quoting 2.9% wide with 8 lots of daily volume left roughly 9% of the credit on the table at the click, and its 0.3185-delta short put only 2.8% below spot would have stacked index short-gamma on a one-day-old position that hasn't yet cleared Jackson Hole. Correct action is to let the existing 765/775 spread work.
  IWM: passed on 6 candidates — Closest was the 283/279 put credit spread (score 56.5, 79.2% PoP, 0.196 short delta). The number that stopped it: max gain is $51 per contract and qty is hard-capped at 1, while round-trip friction on a two-leg spread is ~$15 plus $4.50 of entry slippage — roughly 38% of the entire theoretical premium consumed by costs, against a $349 max loss. At full-loss weighting the credit does not even cover the tail (0.792x51 - 0.208x349 = -$32), and the scoring model stamped event_risk 0.0 despite Jackson Hole and a hot PCE sitting inside a 50-day hold on the most rate-sensitive index on the board. The book is also already short an index call spread in QQQ, so this is added correlated short-vol, not diversification. Everything else was worse: the 300/304 condor sells a 0.4545-delta strike already through the money for a 21.6% PoP, and both call spreads carry bias_fit 0.0. Not worth $15 of certain spread to buy $36 of best-case edge.
