[14:40:50] scan
  SPY: passed on 6 candidates — Closest was the 2026-10-16 736/732 put credit spread (top score 59.57, 0.1985 short delta, 0.792 PoP). The number that stopped me: $47 max gain per contract against ~$15 round-trip friction on two legs plus $4.00 entry slippage, leaving roughly $28 of realizable credit versus $353 of max loss — and on the pack's own PoP the raw expectancy is 0.792x47 - 0.208x353 = -$36 before any of that friction. At the 1-contract concentration cap there is no size at which the edge outgrows its own costs. Secondary reasons: the bias_fit=1.0 that carries the score rests on a MACD input the catalyst read flags as actually bearish, and every candidate shares the 2026-10-16 expiry with the existing short QQQ 765/775 call spread, so a single index gap hits both books at once.
