  QQQ: passed on 6 candidates — Came closest to the 2026-10-16 675/765 iron condor (top score 57.89, POP 0.621, $843 max loss inside the $1,000 cap), but the number that stopped it is max_qty: 0 — the book already holds the QQQ 765/775 call vertical and max_positions_per_underlying is 1, so every candidate here is QQQ and would be rejected outright by underlying-concentration rather than trimmed. Independently, the condor's economics were thin anyway: $157 credit against $843 risk needs roughly an 84% win rate to break even versus a stated 62% POP, and $10 entry slippage plus ~$30 round-trip friction on four legs eats a quarter of the credit; three of the six candidates also reuse the 765 short call we are already short at 4.51, which is added concentration at one strike, not diversification.
