  IWM: passed on 6 candidates — Closest call was the 283/279 put credit spread (score 56.58, PoP 0.786, 0.20 short delta 5.6% below spot). What stopped it: $53 max gain per contract against $347 max loss, with ~$4 entry slippage and roughly $15 round-trip friction on two legs — that is ~36% of the gross credit gone to costs, leaving ~$34 of expected take on a reward/risk sub-score of 0.031. The pack also scores event_risk at 0.0 across a 50-DTE window that contains the Jackson Hole / post-hot-PCE rate path, and IV-regime fit of 0.20 says I am selling cheap premium on the most rate-sensitive index proxy while the tape shows 10 of 11 sectors lower on narrow mega-cap leadership; the bias_fit of 1.0 that lifts this score is the single input the current evidence contradicts. Alternatives were worse: 316/320 and the 283/316 condor quote 6.4% worst-leg width, and the 299/304 condor is 0.164 PoP. Not enough premium to carry short gamma through a rate catalyst.
