[15:11:10] scan
  SPY: passed on 6 candidates — Closest call was the 737/733 put credit spread (top score 58.5, POP 0.79, $357 defined risk), but the arithmetic stopped it: $43 max gain per contract against $8.50 of quoted entry slippage and roughly $15 round-trip friction on a 3.0%-wide, 51-lot/day leg — 35-40% of maximum gain consumed by cost before any tail risk, on an 8.3-to-1 adverse payoff. Sizing cannot fix it since max_qty is 1 and both gain and friction scale together. Secondary reasons: the 800/820 and 800/820-condor variants are dead against the $1,000 per-position cap ($1,734 / $1,691), the 756/752 alternative is worse per dollar (0.32 delta, $10.55 slippage on $70), and the book already holds a QQQ 765/775 call vertical in the same 2026-10-16 cycle, so an SPY put spread would spend a correlated slot for fifty days to net directional exposure toward zero for 5bp of equity. Waiting for a wider credit or a tighter market.
