  QQQ: passed on 6 candidates — Mechanical stop: max_qty is 0 for QQQ (one position per underlying already used by the open 765/775 October call spread), so every candidate here would be rejected outright by the underlying-concentration gate, not trimmed. The one I came closest to was the 675/765 iron condor — it scores highest at 57.71 and its call wing is literally the position we already hold, so the true increment is only the 673/675 put wing for $23 of credit against $177 of risk, which does not cover ~$15 of round-trip friction even before the Jackson Hole / semiconductor-tariff headline risk inside the 50-day window. Leave the existing spread to work.
