  SPY: passed on 6 candidates — Closest call was the 2026-10-16 738/734 put credit spread (top score 59.41, 0.20 short delta, 4.3% cushion, bias-aligned with the mild bullish read and offsetting rather than compounding the existing short QQQ 765/775 call vertical). The number that stopped me: $44 max gain per contract against ~$15 round-trip friction plus $4.50 entry slippage — friction is ~44% of the entire prize — and at $356 risk for $400 width the structure needs an ~89% expiry win rate while the pack itself only claims 79% POP. Sizing cannot fix this: max_qty is 1 and the ratio is per-contract regardless. The 771/767 spread has better reward/risk but sells a 0.4543-delta strike (breakeven 769.41, essentially spot) for a 55% POP against a 60% required win rate, with the worst liquidity and $10.50 slippage in the set; the 800/810 and 800/820 call spreads carry 0.0 bias_fit and would double the book's existing short-upside exposure on a correlated index. No candidate clears its own friction, so the cheapest correct action is to wait for a wider credit or a richer IV regime.
